  [rainy-traffic-hiss-bed] grader rejected: Road width choices are nearly indistinguishable. Alley, street and avenue show the same three broadband pass swells with similar envelopes, and centroids differ only by about 1000-1300 Hz. Nothing reads as a narrow reflective alley versus a wide open avenue (no reverb or slap difference, no change in pass spread or distance). | Each pass is a flat, full-band noise swell from bottom to top. There is no brightening on approach or darkening as it leaves, and no hint of a doppler-like spectral sweep, so it reads as gated noise rather than tyres throwing water. | Wet spray character is weak. The default centroid of about 1 kHz and broadband texture lack the dominant sizzle above 3-4 kHz that sells wet tarmac hiss, and the low rumble band is the hottest element at defaults. | The loop toggle shows no visible effect. The loop=false render looks essentially the same as the default, so the crossfade either does nothing audible or is inaudible at the seams. | At maximum, density, pass rate and rumble pile up into an undifferentiated roar (centroid 735 Hz). Individual passes disappear and it reads as a generic noise bed rather than heavy wet traffic. | At minimum, the program produces one isolated pass in the first second and then roughly 3 s of thin bed. This is usable as sparse traffic, but it is lopsided for a 4 s loop. | Density and pass rate appear to overlap in effect. Both mainly change how many swells occur, so the designer has two knobs doing one job.
